# NFL database: large regenerable artifacts.
# raw/ is ~316 MB of nflverse CSV extracts; cache/ is ~1 GB of cached ESPN, NFL,
# PFR and covers.com responses from the forensic audit. Both are rebuilt by
# scripts/data/nfl-db/build_db.py and the audit/ scripts. The build scripts,
# schema, lib modules and audit reports ARE tracked -- they are the source of truth.
scripts/data/nfl-db/raw/
scripts/data/nfl-db/cache/
# The provenance sidecar describes a LOCAL build of the (untracked) nfl.db, so it
# is untracked for the same reason the database is. Tracking it would also be
# self-poisoning: every build would dirty the worktree, and the NEXT build would
# then correctly stamp itself "not accepted reproducibility evidence" because of
# the artifact the previous build left behind.
scripts/data/nfl-db/*.provenance.json
# NOTE: a negation cannot re-include a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY -- git
# never descends into raw/ to evaluate it. An earlier
# `!scripts/data/nfl-db/raw/EXTRACT-NOTES.md` here was inert and silently kept
# the extract provenance out of the repo. The notes now live one level up, at
# scripts/data/nfl-db/EXTRACT-NOTES.md, where nothing excludes them.
#
# THIS BIT US TWICE. cache/b3/espn_identities.json (9 KB, 39 records) is a build
# INPUT, not a cache: it feeds the crosswalk's T4 tier. Being under cache/ it was
# never in any clone, and build_db.py skipped T4 silently when it was absent --
# so a clean clone built green while 316 audited depth_chart rows quietly lost
# their gsis_id, and the loss looked like upstream drift. It now lives at
# scripts/data/nfl-db/espn-identities.json and its absence is a hard error.
# Before adding anything under raw/ or cache/, ask whether the build READS it. If
# it does, it is an input and belongs outside these directories.

# Forensic audit ledgers: one JSON line per row-level comparison, ~2 GB raw.
# They compress ~37:1, so the .gz form plus the extracted findings are what get
# committed -- those carry every non-clean verdict. Raw .jsonl stays local.
# What IS committed: the gzipped complete ledgers, the per-agent verdict
# summaries, and findings/actionable/ (MISMATCH, DB_ONLY, REF_ONLY -- 18,027
# records anyone must adjudicate). What is NOT: the raw .jsonl, and the
# unfiltered findings/*.jsonl, which are 96 MB dominated by 204,033 UNRESOLVED
# rows all saying the same thing -- Pro-Football-Reference returned 403. That
# count belongs in the summaries, not in a per-row file nobody can read.
docs/audits/2026-07-27-nfl-db-forensic/ledger/*.jsonl
docs/audits/2026-07-27-nfl-db-forensic/ledger/findings/*.jsonl
!docs/audits/2026-07-27-nfl-db-forensic/ledger/*.jsonl.gz
!docs/audits/2026-07-27-nfl-db-forensic/ledger/findings/*.json
!docs/audits/2026-07-27-nfl-db-forensic/ledger/findings/actionable/*.jsonl

